<p>I found this impenetrable thanks to the jargon, especially in regards to the antimemes. The definitions themselves make no sense to me, and all I took away from this was &quot;spooky building, spooky crack, light and noise and the Foundation is an anomaly somehow&quot;. The &quot;only read below if you want <em>The Truth</em>&quot; opener did not help things any.</p>
<p>On a different tack, I feel the formatting was a bad choice, too. Had this been a series of collapsibles instead of a tabview, it might look better, or at least I wouldn't have had to keep scrolling back to the top to find the next tab. I suppose you want the verisimilitude of being able to scroll to the bottom and get the amnestic at any time, but I think it'd be best if you considered putting the reader into the pants of someone who had decided to read the whole thing. As it stands, -1.</p>

